10:["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"🟦 Project mission"}]
11:["$","p","p-5",{"children":"Build repeatable AWS infrastructure using Terraform instead of manually creating every resource in the AWS Console. Learn how to define infrastructure as code, review proposed changes, provision a network and compute resources, protect Terraform state, and clean up resources safely."}]
12:["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"🌈 1. First Understand the Project — Simple Words"}]
13:["$","p","p-6",{"children":"Imagine a company called ShopEasy. It needs a network, a server, and security rules for a small application."}]
14:["$","p","p-7",{"children":"Without Infrastructure as Code, an engineer may create each resource manually in the AWS Console. That can be slow, difficult to reproduce, and easy to configure differently between environments."}]
15:["$","p","p-8",{"children":["With Terraform, the engineer describes the desired infrastructure in ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":".tf"}]," files. Terraform compares the configuration with the current state and creates a plan showing what it intends to change."]}]
16:["$","h3","h3-0",{"children":"🧠 The simplest analogy"}]
17:["$","p","p-9",{"children":"Think of Terraform like a building plan:"}]
18:["$","table","table-0",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{"children":"Building work"}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"AWS / Terraform meaning"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"What it tells us"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"📝 Building blueprint"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Terraform configuration"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"What should exist"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🧱 Plot and roads"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"VPC, subnet, routes"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Where resources connect"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🚪 Entry permissions"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Security groups and IAM"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Who can access what"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🏢 Building"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"EC2 instance"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Compute resource to run a workload"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-4",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🔍 Engineer reviews the plan"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"children":"terraform plan"}]}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"What Terraform intends to change"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-5",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🛠️ Construction"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"children":"terraform apply"}]}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Apply the reviewed changes"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-6",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🗂️ Project records"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Terraform state"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"What Terraform manages"}]]}]]}]]}]
19:["$","p","p-10",{"children":"The analogy is not exact, but it helps explain the workflow: define, review, apply, verify, and maintain infrastructure."}]
1a:["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"🏢 2. Real-World Company Scenario — The Story"}]
1b:["$","h3","h3-1",{"children":"📦 Company situation"}]
1c:["$","p","p-11",{"children":"ShopEasy needs a small AWS environment for a demo application. The team wants a predictable network, a compute instance, and restricted access."}]
1d:["$","p","p-12",{"children":"Before IaC, an engineer might manually create the VPC, subnet, internet gateway, route table, security group, and EC2 instance. Rebuilding the same environment later can require repeating many steps."}]
1e:["$","p","p-13",{"children":"With Terraform, the desired configuration is version-controlled and can be reviewed before changes are applied."}]
1f:["$","h3","h3-2",{"children":"🔴 10:00 AM — Requirement arrives"}]
20:["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Create an isolated VPC."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Add a subnet and route resources."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Create a security group with restricted inbound access."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Provision an EC2 instance."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Tag resources so the team can identify ownership and purpose."}],"\n"]}]
21:["$","h3","h3-3",{"children":"🟠 10:10 AM — Terraform plan is reviewed"}]
22:["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Terraform reads the configuration and current state."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"The engineer reviews resource creation, modification, and deletion."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"The team checks the region, AMI, permissions, network exposure, and estimated cost."}],"\n"]}]
23:["$","h3","h3-4",{"children":"🔴 10:15 AM — A configuration issue is found"}]
24:["$","p","p-14",{"children":["The plan shows SSH access open to ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"0.0.0.0/0"}],". The engineer stops and changes the rule to a specific trusted IP or chooses Systems Manager Session Manager instead."]}]
25:["$","h3","h3-5",{"children":"🟢 10:25 AM — Infrastructure is applied and verified"}]
26:["$","p","p-15",{"children":"After approval, Terraform applies the reviewed plan. The engineer checks the AWS resources and confirms that networking and access settings match the requirement."}]
27:["$","p","p-16",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Important:"}]," This is an illustrative scenario, not evidence that AWS resources have already been created."]}]
28:["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"🎯 3. What Exactly Will We Build?"}]
29:["$","p","p-17",{"children":"We will design a small AWS infrastructure lab managed by Terraform."}]
2a:["$","table","table-1",{"children":[["$","thead","thead-0",{"children":["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","th","th-0",{"children":"Component"}],["$","th","th-1",{"children":"Responsibility"}],["$","th","th-2",{"children":"Simple explanation"}]]}]}],["$","tbody","tbody-0",{"children":[["$","tr","tr-0",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🧰 Terraform"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Infrastructure as Code"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Defines and manages resources through configuration"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-1",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"☁️ AWS Provider"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Connects Terraform to AWS APIs"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Lets Terraform manage supported AWS resources"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-2",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🌐 VPC"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Network boundary"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Provides a logically isolated AWS network"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-3",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🧩 Public Subnet"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Subnet inside the VPC"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Places the demo instance in a selected network range"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-4",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🚪 Internet Gateway"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Internet route target"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Enables internet routing when routes and public addressing are configured"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-5",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🛣️ Route Table"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Network routes"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Decides where matching traffic is sent"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-6",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🛡️ Security Group"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Instance traffic rules"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Controls allowed inbound and outbound traffic"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-7",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🖥️ EC2"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Compute"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Provides a virtual machine for the demo"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-8",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"🔐 IAM"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Identity and access"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Controls which identities can perform AWS actions"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-9",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"📤 Outputs"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"Useful resource values"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Prints IDs and addresses after deployment"}]]}],["$","tr","tr-10",{"children":[["$","td","td-0",{"children":"⚙️ GitHub Actions"}],["$","td","td-1",{"children":"CI validation"}],["$","td","td-2",{"children":"Checks Terraform formatting and configuration on changes"}]]}]]}]]}]
